  "id": "Compound::DB01234 - Disease::DOID:7148",
  "verbalization": "Dexamethasone, through its structural resemblance to Flumethasone Pivalate and Betamethasone, shares a common biological pathway with glucocorticoids, which are known to modulate inflammatory processes. The evidence suggests that Dexamethasone may exert its therapeutic effects through a mechanism involving the 17Alpha-Hydroxy Steroid pathway, which is associated with the regulation of immune responses and inflammation. This pathway is also linked to the treatment of Rheumatoid Arthritis, as Betamethasone is a well-established glucocorticoid used for this condition. The observed relationships highlight a potential mechanism by which Dexamethasone could be repurposed for Rheumatoid Arthritis, likely through its glucocorticoid-like effects on inflammatory pathways. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of glucocorticoid signaling in the pathophysiology of Rheumatoid Arthritis, suggesting that Dexamethasone may offer a viable alternative or adjunct in its treatment.",
